Summarize assembled contigs in FASTA format, plain or compressed, such as contig counts, lengths, and N50. For raw reads, see [Genomic Read Summary](/docs/gui-usage/read-summary/).

## Steps

1. Select `Genomics` in the navigation bar {% ref id="A" /%}.
2. Open `Summarize genomic contigs` from the tool list on wide windows, or select the tool name {% ref id="B" /%} at the top of the page to switch tools.
3. Add the input files {% ref id="C" /%} with `Browse files`, `Browse folder`, or `Open archive`. SEGUI searches a folder and its subfolders for files that match the tool's input format. See [file input](/docs/gui-usage/intro/#file-input) for mobile options.
4. The `Input` tab of the file panel {% ref id="E" /%} lists the input files. On phones and narrow windows, open it with the files button next to the tool name. To remove files from the list, choose `Select`, pick the files, and select `Remove`. The files stay on your device.
5. Select `Browse` under `Select output directory` to choose the output folder. On phones and tablets, enter a `Directory name` instead; SEGUI saves it in the app's own folder.
6. Select the run button {% ref id="D" /%}, labeled `Summarize`, to start the task.
7. Export or share the output (optional). See [exporting output](/docs/gui-usage/intro/#exporting-output).

## Available statistics for contiguous sequences

- Contig count
- Base count
- Nucleotide
- GC content
- AT content
- Minimum contig length
- Maximum contig length
- Mean contig length
- Median contig length
- N50
- N75
- N90
- Contig 750 bp
- Contig 1000 bp
- Contig 1500 bp
- Cumulative length
- A, C, G, T, N counts
